          "text": "The pattern indexes as a primitive hexagonal cell with approximately \\(a=3.387\\) \u00c5 and \\(c=13.236\\) \u00c5. The strong low-angle series is \\(00l\\), while the peaks from 30\u201352\u00b0 follow the \\(10l\\) series. A polar, ordered \\(P3m1\\) model gives the most consistent intensity modulation. The internal coordinates are powder-derived and should be regarded as approximate to about 0.005\u20130.01 in \\(z\\).\n\n```cif\ndata_TaNbCuS4\n_audit_creation_method              'Structure solution from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common               'copper niobium tantalum sulfide'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Cu Nb S4 Ta'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'CuNbTaS4'\n_chemical_formula_weight            465.64\n_cell_formula_units_Z               1\n\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M       'P 3 m 1'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number          156\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt            'P 3 m 1'\n_space_group_IT_number               156\n\n_cell_length_a                       3.3870\n_cell_length_b                       3.3870\n_cell_length_c                       13.2360\n_cell_angle_alpha                    90\n_cell_angle_beta                     90\n_cell_angle_gamma                    120\n_cell_volume                         131.54\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type               'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength         1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-y,x-y,z'\n3  '-x+y,-x,z'\n4  '-x+y,y,z'\n5  '-y,-x,z'\n6  'x,x-y,z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nCu1 Cu 1 a 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000 1.000 0.010\nTa1 Ta 1 a 0.000000 0.000000 0.209000 1.000 0.008\nNb1 Nb 1 b 0.333333 0.666667 0.709000 1.000 0.008\nS1  S  1 b 0.333333 0.666667 0.092500 1.000 0.012\nS2  S  1 b 0.333333 0.666667 0.325500 1.000 0.012\nS3  S  1 a 0.000000 0.000000 0.592500 1.000 0.012\nS4  S  1 a 0.000000 0.000000 0.825500 1.000 0.012\n```\n\nRepresentative indexing is:\n\n| \\(2\\theta\\) (\u00b0) | \\(hkl\\) |\n|---:|:---|\n| 6.67 | 001 |\n| 13.37 | 002 |\n| 20.11 | 003 |\n| 26.92 | 004 |\n| 30.46 | 100 |\n| 31.21 | 101 |\n| 33.39 | 102 |\n| 33.83 | 005 |\n| 36.77 | 103 |\n| 40.87 | 006 |\n| 41.09 | 104 |\n| 46.15 | 105 |\n| 51.81 | 106 |\n| 54.12 | 110 |\n| 55.48 | 112 |\n| 56.01 | 008 |\n\nThe inversion-related opposite-polarity domain is exactly indistinguishable in an unpolarized powder pattern. It is generated from the CIF above by\n\n\\[\n(x,y,z)\\rightarrow(-x,-y,-z),\n\\]\n\nand is therefore not a chemically distinct alternative structure.",
